userStories.description:
**Goal** — Resolve one shared repo/package/override rule set for every delivery path while preserving pipeline static-rule behavior.

**Motivation** — Across 2,006 context manifests since 2026-09-20, `static-rules` is 84% of engine tokens, `feature-context` 10%, `git-history` 3% and `code-neighbor` 1.7%.

**Approach** — Verbatim design: "Layers are applied in order: repo `.nax/rules/`, then package `<pkg>/.nax/rules/`, then the override directory. A later layer replaces an earlier rule with the same rule id. In `replace` mode, only the override layer is used. Override rules are treated like repo-level rules: filtered by `paths:` through `ruleMatchesPackage`, and their literal `appliesTo` entries framed through `frameAppliesTo`." "It finds the file's package (`findPackageDir`), resolves that package's rule set, and keeps the rules whose `appliesTo` matches the file. A rule with no `appliesTo` governs every file."

`loadCanonicalRules(workdir, options)`: "same signature, delegating to a new exported `loadCanonicalRulesFromDir(rulesDir: string, options?: LoadCanonicalRulesOptions): Promise<CanonicalRule[]>`. That function holds today's body, so the depth cap, frontmatter policy and `lintForNeutrality` apply unchanged to any directory."

`StaticRulesProvider.fetch`: "that block becomes one `resolveRuleSet(input, { loadRepoRules: _staticRulesDeps.loadCanonicalRules })` call. Its result carries `rules` plus the pre-filter counts `repoRulesTotal`, `repoRulesMatchedPaths` and `packageRulesCount`, which the `#558` "none apply" branch (`:263-270`) keeps reading unchanged. Under `overrideMode: "replace"` the repo and package layers are not loaded, so all three counts are 0 and that branch cannot fire. `loadRepoRules` serves BOTH the repo and the package layer, so the existing stubs in six test files keep driving `fetch`. The file-private `canonicalRuleId`, `canonicalRulePath` and `canonicalRulePriority` (`:106-116`) move to the rule-set module and are imported back. The stage, `appliesTo` and budget logic after the block is unchanged. The file is at 591/600 lines, and the extraction must leave it smaller."

`StaticRulesProvider` constructor options: "gains optional `overrideDir?: string` and `overrideMode?: "merge" | "replace"`, forwarded to `resolveRuleSet`." `createDefaultOrchestrator`: "passes `config.context?.rules?.overrideDir` and `config.context?.rules?.overrideMode` into the `StaticRulesProvider` options."

Use `ruleMatchesScopeFiles` with one file and the existing path helpers unchanged; `findPackageDir` returns a repo-relative package identity. Reuse memoized repo loading, independently memoize override-directory loads and evict rejected promises. Avoid a load-time cycle with static-rules when sharing the matcher. New production consumers import the nested barrel by exact alias `@/context/rules/rule-set`. New tests go in new files; do not grow static-rules.test.ts or change its existing loader seam.

**Scope** — In: canonical directory loader extraction, layer merge/filter/frame/display metadata, file governance resolution and static-provider/orchestrator wiring. Out: US-002 owns config/CLI/setup validation; US-003 owns index prompts; US-005 owns native session delivery; US-006 owns review maps; US-007 owns project context. Pipeline mode (`execution.mode: "pipeline"`, frozen since 2026-10-16) is unchanged. It keeps `contextStage`, the v2 orchestrator and rule pushing; only the rules override directory reaches it, through `StaticRulesProvider`.

**Interface** — Verbatim TypeScript:
```typescript
export type RuleSource = "repo" | "package" | "override";
export interface ResolvedRule extends CanonicalRule {
  readonly ruleId: string;       // canonicalRuleId(rule)
  readonly source: RuleSource;
  readonly displayPath: string;  // ".nax/rules/<rel>", "<storyWorkdir>/.nax/rules/<rel>", or the absolute override path
}
export interface ResolveRuleSetInput {
  readonly repoRoot: string;
  readonly packageDir: string;    // absolute; equals repoRoot for the root package
  readonly storyWorkdir?: string; // repo-relative package frame
  readonly overrideDir?: string;  // absolute
  readonly overrideMode?: "merge" | "replace"; // default "merge"
}
export interface RuleLoaders {
  /** Loads `<workdir>/.nax/rules`, for the repo layer AND the package layer. Default: memoized `loadCanonicalRules` (key: workdir). */
  readonly loadRepoRules?: (workdir: string) => Promise<CanonicalRule[]>;
  /** Loads an override directory. Default: memoized `loadCanonicalRulesFromDir` (key: absolute dir). */
  readonly loadDirRules?: (dir: string) => Promise<CanonicalRule[]>;
}
export interface ResolvedRuleSet {
  readonly rules: readonly ResolvedRule[];
  readonly repoRulesTotal: number;        // repo rules before the paths: filter
  readonly repoRulesMatchedPaths: number; // repo rules after the paths: filter
  readonly packageRulesCount: number;     // package-layer rules loaded (0 at the root)
}
export function resolveRuleSet(input: ResolveRuleSetInput, loaders?: RuleLoaders): Promise<ResolvedRuleSet>;
export interface RulesForFileInput {
  readonly repoRoot: string;
  readonly path: string;          // repo-relative, normalized
  readonly overrideDir?: string;
  readonly overrideMode?: "merge" | "replace";
}
export function rulesForFile(input: RulesForFileInput, loaders?: RuleLoaders): Promise<ResolvedRule[]>;
export function canonicalRuleId(rule: CanonicalRule): string;
export function canonicalRulePath(rule: CanonicalRule): string;
export function canonicalRulePriority(rule: CanonicalRule): number;
export function loadCanonicalRulesFromDir(rulesDir: string, options?: LoadCanonicalRulesOptions): Promise<CanonicalRule[]>;
```

**Goal** — Add root-scoped rules/project-context configuration and CLI paths, and validate the rules directory before configuring run handlers.

**Motivation** — An orchestrator that runs `nax run` across many repos cannot supply organisation-wide or per-job rules or project context without committing them into each target repo.

**Approach** — Verbatim design: "Each is declared as `XBase.default(() => XBase.parse({}))`, like `TestCoverageConfigSchema` (`:23`), because `NaxConfigSchema` re-parses `ContextConfigSchema.parse({})` for its default (`packages/nax/src/config/schemas.ts:349`)." `pinRootOnlyKeys`: "returns `context: { ...merged.context, rules: root.context.rules, projectContext: root.context.projectContext }`, leaving every other `context.*` key as merged." `pinRootOnlyKeysRaw`: "when `raw.context.rules` or `raw.context.projectContext` differs from the root value (`Bun.deepEquals`), calls `onIgnored` once naming the key and replaces only that sub-key, spreading the rest of `raw.context` unchanged."

`RunActionOptions` gains `rulesDir?: string` and `contextFile?: string`. `resolveRunProjectContext`: "maps `options.rulesDir` to `cliOverrides.context.rules.overrideDir`, and `options.contextFile` to `cliOverrides.context.projectContext.file`. An absolute or `~/` value passes through unchanged; anything else becomes `join(workdir, value)`." The run command "adds `--rules-dir <path>` and `--context-file <path>`. The project-context flag is NOT `--context`, because `--no-context` (`:220`) already defines `options.context` as a boolean."

`initializeAfterLock`: "`runtime.sessionManager.configureLoopHandlers(await configureRunRules({ config, workdir, pluginHandlers: pluginRegistry.getLoopHandlers() }))`. All new branching lives in `configureRunRules`, because `initializeAfterLock` is baselined at complexity 21 (`scripts/baselines/complexity-baseline.json:73`) and `bun run check:complexity` allows no growth. `InitializeAfterLockDeps` is unchanged." At this story's completion configureRunRules returns the original plugin set by identity after validation; US-005 adds handlers, and US-007 adds project-file validation.

Verbatim file-format rules: "`context.rules.delivery`: `"index"` (default) or `"push"`. `"push"` restores today's workflow behaviour. `contextStage` runs the v2 orchestrator, the brief carries the rule bodies, and no rule-delivery handlers or review-package rules sections are produced." "`context.rules.overrideDir`: optional." "Must be absolute or start with `~/`; `~/` expands to the home directory." "A relative value fails config validation. On the CLI, see `resolveRunProjectContext` above." "The directory has the layout and frontmatter of `.nax/rules/`." "`context.rules.overrideMode`: `"merge"` (default) or `"replace"`." "`context.projectContext.file`: optional, with the same path rules as `overrideDir`. A Markdown file of at most 32,768 bytes." "`context.projectContext.mode`: `"append"` (default) or `"replace"`." "All these keys are settable in global config, project config, a profile and on the CLI. The repo is inside nax's trust boundary (`docs/architecture/agent-adapters.md` §17, D-1), so no layer is rejected." "A per-package `.nax/mono/<pkg>/config.json` cannot change them (root-only pinning)."

Failure handling: "`overrideDir` configured but missing or not a directory at run start" → "`configureRunRules` throws `NaxError` code `RULES_OVERRIDE_DIR_NOT_FOUND` (context `stage: "run-setup"`, `overrideDir`) before any story runs. Fail-closed: the operator asked for those rules." Validate independently of delivery mode and preserve setup's existing lock cleanup on throw. Add config-descriptions entries. Consumers read the new keys defensively (`config.context?.rules?.delivery ?? "index"`), matching the existing `context?.v2?.` reads, so sparse test configs do not throw.

**Scope** — In: new config defaults/path validation/home expansion, selective root-only pinning, flags/CLI path translation, helper and setup integration. Out: US-001 resolves/loads rule content; US-003 renders indexes; US-004 changes workflow context assembly; US-005 adds native handlers; US-007 validates/loads/delivers project-context content and warns about replace mode.

**Interface** — Verbatim TypeScript, introducing only dirExists on the dependency object in this story and adding the annotated entries in their owning downstream stories:
```typescript
export const _runRulesSetupDeps: {
  dirExists: (path: string) => Promise<boolean>;
  loadProjectContextOverride: typeof loadProjectContextOverride; // US-007
  createRuleDeliveryHandlers: typeof createRuleDeliveryHandlers; // US-005
};
/** Validates both overrides (throws before returning); returns the set for configureLoopHandlers. */
export function configureRunRules(input: { config: NaxConfig; workdir: string; pluginHandlers: LoopHandlerSet }): Promise<LoopHandlerSet>;
```
Target configuration shape:
```json
{
  "context": {
    "rules": {
      "delivery": "index",
      "overrideDir": "/abs/path/to/org-rules",
      "overrideMode": "merge"
    },
    "projectContext": {
      "file": "~/fleet/contexts/strict-unattended.md",
      "mode": "append"
    }
  }
}
```
